1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:32,256
Welcome to the Accountabul Lending Protocol Live DevNet Lab. DevNet assets only — nothing here is real money.

2
00:00:32,706 --> 00:00:45,378
STEP 1 OF 8 — Fund the required wallets. Every XRPL account needs XRP for reserves and fees.

3
00:00:45,828 --> 00:00:54,276
Vault Owner / Loan Broker — creates the vault and manages the Loan Broker.

4
00:00:54,726 --> 00:01:03,486
Depositor — provides liquidity and receives vault shares, not ownership of the vault.

5
00:01:03,936 --> 00:01:11,712
Borrower — receives capital and repays according to the agreed terms.

6
00:01:12,162 --> 00:01:42,450
Fund All Wallets. Not Funded becomes Funded after the ledger verifies the faucet drop.

7
00:01:42,900 --> 00:02:05,244
Reset DevNet Lab clears the browser session. New session ≠ erase ledger.

8
00:02:05,694 --> 00:02:19,134
STEP 2 OF 8 — Create the lending vault. One pool. One asset. Shares for depositors.

9
00:02:19,584 --> 00:02:30,672
Vault Asset = XRP. A single-asset vault does not mix currencies.

10
00:02:31,122 --> 00:02:45,738
Maximum Capacity: 100,000 — deposits cannot exceed this ceiling.

11
00:02:46,188 --> 00:03:17,004
Create Vault → Preparing → Signing → Submitting → Validating → tesSUCCESS. Verify the Vault object on DevNet.

12
00:03:17,454 --> 00:03:36,006
STEP 3 OF 8 — Deposit liquidity. The lab checks vault, funding, asset, and remaining capacity first.

13
00:03:36,456 --> 00:03:49,536
Deposit 10,000. Before: vault assets 0. After tesSUCCESS: vault assets 10,000.

14
00:03:49,986 --> 00:04:14,082
Depositor → Assets → Vault → Vault Shares → Depositor. Shares are a claim on the pool, not a guaranteed return.

15
00:04:14,532 --> 00:04:46,308
Protocol Loan Book = application view. LoanBroker = XRPL protocol object.

16
00:04:46,758 --> 00:05:13,878
Create Loan Broker. Empty book: No loans yet. Originate your first loan.

17
00:05:14,328 --> 00:05:20,904
STEP 5 OF 8 — Originate a loan. The borrower requests capital from the vault via the Loan Broker.

18
00:05:21,354 --> 00:05:40,842
Principal 10,000 · APR 10% · Term 12 months · Payment frequency monthly.

19
00:05:41,292 --> 00:05:56,052
Loan Broker signs, then Borrower signs. Both must agree before LoanSet is submitted.

20
00:05:56,502 --> 00:06:23,958
Originate Loan → LoanSet → tesSUCCESS. Vault → Loan → Borrower. Available assets fall.

21
00:06:24,408 --> 00:06:35,880
STEP 6 OF 8 — Make a loan payment. Outstanding principal 10,000. A payment is due.

22
00:06:36,330 --> 00:07:08,946
Borrower → Loan → Vault. Principal reduces the balance. Interest is the cost of borrowing — not a guaranteed return.

23
00:07:09,396 --> 00:07:30,996
STEP 7 OF 8 — Withdraw. Assets Total ≠ Assets Available. Only available liquidity can be redeemed.

24
00:07:31,446 --> 00:07:52,422
Vault Shares → Vault → Assets → Depositor. Redeem shares for available assets only.

25
00:07:52,872 --> 00:08:25,008
Deposit Failed · tecNO_AUTH · The account is not authorized for this action. Read the code, then fix, then retry.

26
00:08:25,458 --> 00:09:00,018
STEP 8 OF 8 — Verify the ledger. Confirm the interface and the XRP Ledger agree.

27
00:09:00,468 --> 00:09:14,652
View Technical Details: hash, ledger index, type, result, validated. Proof lives on the ledger.

28
00:09:15,102 --> 00:09:41,766
Correct order: Fund → Vault → Deposit → Loan Broker → Originate → Pay → Withdraw → Verify.

29
00:09:42,216 --> 00:10:12,120
Fund → Vault → Deposit → Loan Broker → Originate → Pay → Withdraw → Verify. Learn it. Test it. Verify it on XRPL.

